{"id": "EUVD-2026-86868", "enisaUuid": "b4698167-682a-39e6-8fc4-f182c3a68e27", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix one-byte OOB read in smb2_parse_native_symlink()\n\nWhen parsing a share-root relative native symlink, memcpy copies\nsmb_target+1 (skipping the leading separator) but uses\nstrlen(smb_target)+1 as the length, reading one byte past the\nallocated buffer.\n\nThis fixes the following KASAN splat when accessing an SMB symlink\nwith a target of '\\a\\b':\n\n  BUG: KASAN: slab-out-of-bounds in smb2_parse_native_symlink+0x4f5/0xca0\n  Read of size 5 at addr ffff88800878fe21 by task netfsfuzz-execu/1\n  CPU: 1 UID: 0 PID: 1 Comm: netfsfuzz-execu Tainted: G N\n  7.2.0-11943-g2709dd5ae32f-dirty #1 PREEMPT(lazy)\n  Hardware name: QEMU Ubuntu 24.04 PC v2 (i440FX + PIIX, arch_caps fix,\n  1996)\n  Call Trace:\n   <TASK>\n   dump_stack_lvl+0x7b/0xa0\n   print_report+0xd0/0x630\n   kasan_report+0xe5/0x120\n   kasan_check_range+0x105/0x1b0\n   __asan_memcpy+0x23/0x60\n   smb2_parse_native_symlink+0x4f5/0xca0\n   parse_reparse_point+0x68a/0x1530\n   reparse_info_to_fattr+0x752/0xa20\n   cifs_get_fattr+0x873/0x15b0\n   cifs_get_inode_info+0xc0/0x310\n   cifs_lookup+0x308/0xa70\n   __lookup_slow+0x122/0x2b0\n   lookup_slow+0x50/0x70\n   path_lookupat+0x525/0xaf0\n   filename_lookup+0x1f2/0x550\n   vfs_statx+0xd1/0x1a0\n   vfs_fstatat+0x65/0xc0\n   __do_sys_newfstatat+0x9a/0x120\n   do_syscall_64+0xdd/0x4a0\n   entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe+0x77/0x7f", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:21:49", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff411fcbfc55eec1d66ea82483d254319dc8e973", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/22a9d0a9ba0c89be57558c1aa80dc60a571dd89c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d1f173d28e964ba2c3c4ebe7491d594dc8c77a40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a302fdbaf7dd00d285303c94af8f48321c22993", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb26524ef4ac28fcfa554c0656e8dc412c38a8ff"], "aliases": ["GHSA-xc88-j6q5-vwwx", "CVE-2026-97560"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02c670e0-1570-35c0-afc1-288ecdefb631", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "1698d481-4440-308a-9b34-f3433763cff0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "723f4ef90452aa629f3d923e92e0449d69362b1d <2a302fdbaf7dd00d285303c94af8f48321c22993"}, {"id": "19b8b16f-ad80-342d-9639-7e005445ea24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "33d840a7-de0c-32f7-9706-61c149c72837", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.2 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "38c36b31-dddd-38bc-94ec-934992e34fb3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "723f4ef90452aa629f3d923e92e0449d69362b1d <cb26524ef4ac28fcfa554c0656e8dc412c38a8ff"}, {"id": "4826d1e3-26ed-3e12-aa39-fbdddd30ca60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "48bcfdee-63dd-3e78-8b4c-0223370fa0af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9280c017ea13ff8678ef4f1ea78a4b683292e8b"}, {"id": "56d193a7-ad82-3f8c-a463-63032d51fa57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "6dac8c5c-f040-3925-9c3f-3733dcab1eac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "723f4ef90452aa629f3d923e92e0449d69362b1d <d1f173d28e964ba2c3c4ebe7491d594dc8c77a40"}, {"id": "865230f9-ff36-326b-bd50-7c6d853c0f68", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "8d17ecf5-233b-3b44-84cc-904bec38bd49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fc5a409552be479715b147748f2f61b41b512976 <22a9d0a9ba0c89be57558c1aa80dc60a